All credit for the dashboard design, the rpcd backend architecture (session
lock, cache, bounded staleness, history), the Realtek diag/OMCI parsers and the
LuCI views belongs to the original authors. This fork adapts that work to a
different device; it is not affiliated with or endorsed by them, by HSGQ, or by ODI.

Changes made in this fork (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)):

  Naming
  - Package, UCI config, ubus object, cache/history/lock files, LuCI menu and
    ACL renamed vsol_ddm -> hsgq_ddm so both tools can be installed side by side.

  Backend (root/usr/libexec/rpcd/hsgq_ddm)
  - Login flow rewritten for the stick's Linux telnetd + login(1): username and
    password are paced instead of pipelined, then each Realtek diag command runs
    one-shot ("diag <cmd>") from the "#" shell instead of inside a vendor CLI.
  - Device facts (uptime, load average, kernel/firmware, MAC) read from Linux
    (/proc/uptime via the shell's read builtin, /proc/loadavg, /proc/version,
    /sys/class/net/eth0/address) because the stick has no "show version".
  - T-CONT queries extended to alloc-IDs 336-339 in addition to 256-259.
  - SFP host-port traffic counters read from "diag mib dump counter port 0".
  - OMCI read directly in the "#" shell (no vendor "AP#" prompt).
  - Restart uses Linux "reboot".
  - Whole-second sleeps only: BusyBox sleep on OpenWrt rejects fractions.
  - Timeout default 20 s (a full session takes ~9 s), cache TTL 10 s,
    max stale 45 s, lock wait 20 s.

  Parser (root/usr/share/hsgq_ddm/parse.awk)
  - Added: uptime, load average, firmware/kernel, SFP MIB counters.
  - Model taken from the optic's vendor + part number (e.g. "ODI DFP-34X-2C2").
  - Device vendor reported as HSGQ.

  LuCI views (htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/hsgq_ddm)
  - Ethernet card replaced by "SFP Host Interface & Traffic" (an SFP ONU has
    no RJ45 ports; removed LAN 1G and management-link rows).
  - System card labels adapted (Kernel, CPU load averages).
  - Settings: timeout range 15-30 s, default 20 s; texts adapted.
  - Removed purge of the original's localStorage keys.

  Packaging
  - New install.sh / uninstall.sh for installing without the OpenWrt SDK.
  - New uci-defaults and CI workflow adapted from the original.
